    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6924": {
      "title": "HDR Engagement and Development Officer",
      "description": "HDR Engagement and Development Officer - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs HDR Engagement and Development Officer Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) — a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The HDR Engagement and Development Officer plays a key role in supporting the delivery of development, training and engagement programs for Higher Degree by Research (HDR) candidates and their supervisors. Working closely with the Engagement and Development Coordinator, you will provide operational and administrative support to ensure workshops, events, communications and learning resources are delivered effectively, contributing to a high-quality HDR experience and a thriving research culture at UOW. Key responsibilities: Coordinate the delivery of HDR workshops, training sessions and engagement activities, ensuring a seamless participant experience across face-to-face, online and hybrid formats. Develop and distribute communications that promote HDR development opportunities and support engagement with students and supervisors. Maintain and update HDR development resources, records and digital platforms, including Moodle, websites and program materials. Provide responsive administrative support, managing enquiries, registrations, event logistics and post-event reporting while ensuring compliance with University policies and procedures. About the Team The School of Graduate Research and Research Culture sits within UOW's Research & Innovation portfolio and provides end-to-end support for Higher Degree by Research candidates throughout their research journey. The team works closely with HDR students, supervisors, academic leaders and professional staff across the University to enhance the HDR experience, support researcher development, and foster a culture of research excellence, integrity and innovation. What You'll Bring A relevant qualification and/or an equivalent combination of education, training and administrative experience. Proven experience providing high-quality administrative or operational support in a busy and complex environment. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and maintain attention to detail. Experience coordinating events, workshops or training activities, including participant communications and logistics. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively with diverse groups and maintain information across digital platforms. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Permanent, Continuing Full-time appointment Level 5: Salary commencing from 85,682 + 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus This position is not suitable for remote working arrangements. Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a resume and a cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Engagement and Development Coordinator, Katie Masonwells masonwells@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Wednesday 16 September 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender Based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender Based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University's employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6924 Job Category Marketing, Communications & Advancement Posting Date 09/01/2026, 10:46 PM Apply Before 09/16/2026, 06:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page HDR Engagement and Development Officer - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
    },
    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6920": {
      "title": "Admissions Officer (Systems)",
      "description": "Admissions Officer (Systems) - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Admissions Officer (Systems) Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Admissions Officer (Systems) plays a key role in ensuring the smooth operation of UOW's admissions systems, processes, and workflows, with a particular focus on the StudyLink admissions platform. Supporting the end-to-end admissions function, this position contributes to accurate, compliant, and efficient application processing while driving operational improvements and maintaining a high-quality experience for prospective students and stakeholders. Key responsibilities: Maintain admissions systems, workflows, processes, and operational documentation to support efficient and compliant admissions outcomes. Coordinate the review, triage, and resolution of operational and system issues, working closely with technical teams and stakeholders. Analyse admissions data and prepare reports that support operational improvements and informed decision-making. Support testing, implementation, and enhancement of admissions systems and related technologies. Contribute to business continuity by delivering training, improving processes, and assisting with admissions assessment activities during peak periods. About the Team The position sits within the Admissions Operations team in the Admissions and Compliance Division and reports to the Manager, Admissions Operations. The team is responsible for delivering efficient, accurate, and student-focused admissions services while ensuring systems, processes, and policies support a seamless admissions experience. The role works closely with Admissions staff, Student Systems, Data and Analytics, IMTS, UOW College, project teams, and external vendors. What You'll Bring A bachelor's degree and relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and professional experience. Demonstrated experience maintaining and improving operational processes and administrative workflows. Strong systems capability, including experience working with databases, reporting tools, and digital platforms. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to develop documentation, deliver training, and engage with a broad range of stakeholders. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Full-time, fixed term to end December 2026 Level 5 | $85,682 - $96,898 per annum + 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus/Hybrid Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the 'Apply Now' button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Harish Kotwal, Senior Project Manager hkotwal@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Monday 14 September 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6920 Job Category Student Services Posting Date 08/31/2026, 11:45 PM Apply Before 09/14/2026, 06:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Admissions Officer (Systems) - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
    },
    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6932": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Project Coordinator - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Project Coordinator Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Project Coordinator plays a key role in delivering refurbishment, renewal and capital works projects across the University’s diverse property portfolio. Reporting to the Project Delivery Manager, you will manage projects through the full lifecycle, from concept development and design through to construction completion and defects liability, ensuring projects are delivered safely, on time, within budget and aligned with University objectives. This is an opportunity to contribute to the enhancement of UOW’s teaching, research and community spaces while working with a broad range of stakeholders. Key responsibilities: Lead the planning, coordination and delivery of refurbishment and capital works projects from inception to completion. Develop project briefs, scopes and budget estimates that support the University’s asset replacement and capital management programs. Procure, engage and manage consultants, contractors and specialist service providers to achieve project outcomes. Manage project governance, risk, contract administration, reporting, quality assurance and stakeholder engagement throughout the project lifecycle. About the Team The Infrastructure and Property Division is responsible for the planning, development, maintenance and enhancement of the University’s built environment and grounds. The team delivers a diverse portfolio of projects, including major refurbishments, asset renewals, functional upgrades and strategic infrastructure initiatives that support teaching, research and student experience outcomes. Working collaboratively across the University, the Division is committed to providing safe, sustainable and high-quality facilities for our community. What You’ll Bring Relevant tertiary qualifications in engineering, construction management, asset management, project management or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of qualifications and experience. Demonstrated experience delivering refurbishment, construction, infrastructure or capital works projects in complex stakeholder environments. Proven project management capability, including procurement, consultant and contractor management, contract administration and budget oversight. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication and relationship management skills, with the ability to influence and collaborate across diverse groups. Sound knowledge of workplace health and safety requirements and a commitment to delivering safe project outcomes. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation. 35‑hour full‑time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family‑friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Fixed Term, Full-time appointment (2 years) Level 6/7: $96,898 - $119,986 plus 17% superannuation. Salary commensurate with skills, experience and capability. Location: Wollongong Campus. Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. A current Australian Driver Licence is required. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a resume and a cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Project Manager, Luke McNamara lukemcn@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Tuesday 15 September 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender Based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender Based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6932 Job Category Business Transformation Posting Date 08/31/2026, 09:38 PM Apply Before 09/15/2026, 06:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Project Coordinator - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
