    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6935": {
      "title": "School Operations Assistant, Engineering",
      "description": "School Operations Assistant, Engineering - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs School Operations Assistant, Engineering Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) — a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally, with more than 33,000 students from over 130 countries. About the Role The School Operations Assistant provides high-quality administrative and operational support to ensure the efficient day-to-day functioning of a School. Working as part of a collaborative professional services team, you will support key academic and business activities, coordinate meetings and events, maintain records and systems, and provide responsive support to a diverse range of stakeholders. This role contributes to a positive staff and student experience while supporting broader Faculty and School initiatives. Key responsibilities: Provide efficient administrative support including diary management, document preparation, record keeping and data management. Coordinate meetings, workshops, seminars and committee activities, ensuring smooth planning and delivery. Support financial and operational processes including purchase orders, invoices, travel arrangements and office resource management. Maintain accurate records, support academic and school processes, and contribute to the delivery of Faculty and School initiatives. About the Team This position sits within the School Operations team and reports to the School Operations Manager or School Coordinator. You will work closely with Heads of School, academic staff, professional services colleagues, Faculty leaders and central business units across the University. The team plays a critical role in enabling teaching, research and operational excellence by delivering responsive, customer-focused support services. What You'll Bring Completion of Year 12, a Certificate II/III in Business Administration (or related discipline), or an equivalent combination of experience and training. Demonstrated experience providing administrative support in a busy and complex office environment. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with a commitment to customer service excellence. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and the ability to maintain accuracy and attention to detail across multiple systems. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Permanent/Continuing, Full-time appointment Level 3/4: $67,214 - $85,682 Salary plus 17% superannuation commensurate with skills, experience and capability Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available Position Description How to Apply Click on the Apply Now button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be requested to submit a resume and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Acting School Operations Manager, Monica Bain mbain@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Wednesday 23 September 2026 11.55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender Based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender Based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University's employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6935 Job Category Administration Posting Date 09/08/2026, 07:14 PM Apply Before 09/23/2026, 06:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs School Operations Coordinator Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 08/25/2026 See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page School Operations Assistant, Engineering - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
