g world-class education and addressing national and global challenges through research and engagement. What You'll Bring A relevant doctoral qualification, or significant professional experience with demonstrated progress towards completion of a doctoral qualification in a relevant field. A strong track record of research achievement and demonstrated capacity to contribute to high-impact research outcomes. Experience in teaching and coordinating subjects in Management, AI and Innovation or related disciplines within higher education. Demonstrated ability to engage effectively in academic governance, service and professional activities. Expertise in one or more areas including Professional Communication, Innovation, Business Transformation, Applied AI and/or Governance. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Permanent/Continuing, Full-time Classification: Level C | Salary Range: $151,746 - $171,141 +17% superannuation Location: Wollongong, Sydney CBD, Liverpool, Sutherland, UOW Online May be required to work outside of standard business hours or across campuses and research partner facilities. Classes in the School of Business are often held evenings and weekends across multiple campuses and online. Work Rights: Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. 