    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6813": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, Project Management, AI & Business Analytics",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer, Project Management, AI & Business Analytics - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Senior Lecturer, Project Management, AI & Business Analytics Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. Join a collaborative and internationally connected business school committed to responsible management education, research excellence and real-world impact About the Role The School of Business is seeking an accomplished Senior Lecturer in Project Management, AI and Business Analytics to contribute to excellence in research, teaching and academic leadership. This continuing position offers the opportunity to undertake high-quality research while delivering innovative undergraduate and postgraduate teaching across Project Management, AI and Business Analytics disciplines. You will play a key role in shaping curriculum, enhancing the student experience, pursuing impactful research, and contributing to the School's strategic ambitions and global impact Key responsibilities: Lead the design, delivery, quality assurance and continuous improvement of undergraduate and postgraduate subjects in the areas of Project Management, AI Strategy and Governance and Business Analytics. Coordinate teaching teams to ensure a high-quality student learning experience, oversee assessment design and moderation processes, and ensure compliance with university and accreditation requirements. Conduct high-quality research within your area of expertise and contribute to major research projects, including leadership opportunities where appropriate. Pursue competitive research funding opportunities and develop collaborations with industry, government and community stakeholders. Foster an inclusive, supportive and technology-enhanced learning environment that promotes student success. Supervise honours and postgraduate research students and contribute to School, Faculty and University governance and service activities About the Team The School of Business is part of the Faculty of Arts, Society and Business and comprises six disciplines: Accounting, Economics, Finance, Management, Supply Chain and Business Analytics, and Marketing. The School is committed to Responsible Management Education and impactful research and holds AACSB accreditation alongside a range of professional accreditations. The School delivers programs across multiple campuses and online and works closely with UOW's international campuses and transnational education partners. This role will join the Supply Chain Management and Business Analytics discipline within a collaborative academic community dedicated to delivering world-class education and addressing national and global challenges through research and engagement What You'll Bring A relevant doctoral qualification, or significant professional experience coupled with demonstrated progress towards completion of a doctoral qualification in a relevant field. Demonstrated skills, knowledge and experience relevant to Supply Chain Management, Business Analytics, Project Management, AI or related disciplines. A significant research track record and demonstrated capacity to contribute to high-impact research outcomes. Demonstrated experience in subject coordination and teaching within higher education. Demonstrated participation in, or capacity to contribute to, governance and service activities within the University and professional bodies. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Supply Chain Management, Business Analytics, Project Management, Applied Machine Learning and AI for Business. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Role Details Employment type: Permanent/Continuing, Full-time Classification: Level C | Salary Range: $151,746 - $171,141 +17% superannuation Location: Wollongong, Sydney CBD, Liverpool, Sutherland, UOW Online May be required to work outside of standard business hours or across campuses and research partner facilities. Classes in the School of Business are often held evenings and weekends across multiple campuses and online. Work Rights: Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Associate Professor, Belinda Gibbons bgibbons@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Monday 28 September 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender-based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender-based Violence during previous employment, or otherwise through a legal process. Any declaration will be treated with strict confidence and in accordance with applicable privacy legislation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6813 Job Category Academia Posting Date 09/14/2026, 11:12 PM Apply Before 09/28/2026, 06:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Senior Lecturer, Management Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 09/15/2026 The School of Business is seeking an accomplished Senior Lecturer in Management, AI and Innovation to contribute to excellence in research, teaching and academic leadership. Senior Lecturer, Molecular Biology Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 09/11/2026 School of Science | Faculty of Science, Medicine and Health See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Senior Lecturer, Project Management, AI & Business Analytics - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
    },
