    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6961": {
      "title": "Risk Systems and Controls Analyst",
      "description": "Risk Systems and Controls Analyst - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Risk Systems and Controls Analyst Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) — a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Risk Systems and Controls Analyst plays a key role in supporting the University’s Risk and Compliance Management Uplift Program. Working within the Legal, Assurance and Integrity Division, you will contribute to the implementation of new controls management capabilities within the Protecht GRC platform, helping to strengthen risk, compliance and assurance practices across the University. This is an exciting opportunity to support enterprise-wide initiatives that improve governance, controls management and organisational resilience. Key responsibilities: Support the implementation and migration of the University’s Controls Register within the Protecht platform, ensuring accurate, complete and fit-for-purpose control information. Facilitate control review, validation and mapping activities with stakeholders across faculties, divisions and controlled entities. Coordinate testing, user acceptance activities and continuous improvement initiatives that enhance risk, compliance and controls management processes. Develop user guidance, training materials and implementation support resources to drive system adoption and successful project outcomes. About the Team The Risk Systems and Controls Analyst sits within the Risk, Compliance and Assurance Unit, part of the Integrity, Legal and Governance Division in the Vice President Operations Portfolio. The team works collaboratively across the University to strengthen risk management, compliance and assurance capability in an increasingly complex and highly regulated environment. Working closely with the Senior Manager, Risk and Assurance, Compliance Manager and a broad range of stakeholders, the team is leading significant initiatives to optimise the University’s Governance, Risk and Compliance systems and establish a more integrated approach to controls management. What You'll Bring A degree in business, information systems, risk management, compliance, governance or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of qualifications and relevant experience. Experience supporting Governance, Risk and Compliance (GRC) systems,  Protecht or a similar platform. Demonstrated experience contributing to system enhancement, process improvement or implementation projects, including testing, documentation, data migration and stakeholder engagement. Knowledge of risk, compliance, controls management, assurance or internal audit practices within a complex organisation. Strong analytical, communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work collaboratively across diverse stakeholder groups. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Fixed term, full-time appointment (15 months) Level 6/7: $96,898 - $119,989 plus 17% superannuation commensurate with experience and capability Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply You are requested to submit a resume and a cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Senior Manager, Risk and Assurance Alexandra Groot-Koerkamp risk-assurance@uow.edu.au The successful candidate will be required to undertake a National Criminal History Check as part of this role. Closing Date: Monday 5 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6961 Job Category Legal & Compliance Posting Date 09/16/2026, 06:58 PM Apply Before 10/05/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Risk Systems and Controls Analyst - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
    },
    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7011": {
      "title": "Director, Legal and Policy",
      "description": "Director, Legal and Policy - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Director, Legal and Policy Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role This is a newly designed leadership opportunity that brings together Legal Services, Policy and Information Compliance into a single strategic portfolio. Reporting to the Chief Legal and Assurance Officer and Secretary to Council, the Director, Legal and Policy will provide enterprise-wide leadership across legal advice, policy governance, privacy, records management and information compliance. As a trusted adviser to senior executives and key decision-makers, you will help shape the University's legal and governance landscape, providing strategic advice on complex legal, regulatory and institutional matters while driving continuous improvement across policy and compliance frameworks. This role offers significant leadership scope, with responsibility for five direct reports and an overall team of 17 staff. You will lead a multidisciplinary team comprising legal, policy and information compliance professionals, setting the strategic direction of the function while fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation, accountability and service excellence. Your direct reports include: Senior Legal Counsel (x2) Paralegal Senior Manager, Information Compliance Policy Remediation Lead This is a unique opportunity to lead a newly integrated function, influence organisational decision-making and establish a contemporary operating model that supports the University's strategic priorities. About the Team The Integrity, Legal and Governance Division is UOW's central function for legal services, governance, risk and compliance, assurance, wellbeing, integrity, secretariat services, complaints and community safety. The Division works closely with the Vice-Chancellor, University Council, University Executive Board and stakeholders across all faculties and divisions and plays a critical role in how UOW governs itself, manages risk and upholds its obligations to staff, students and the broader community. This is a division in an exciting period of growth and is expanding its capability and strengthening the way its functions are organised and led. As Director, Legal and Policy, you will lead one of the Division's two Director-level functions; bringing together Legal Services, Policy and Information Compliance under a single, integrated leadership structure for the first time. You will inherit a capable and experienced team and have the opportunity to shape how legal, policy and information governance services are delivered across a complex, multi-campus institution. This is a role for a senior leader who wants to do more than manage a legal function — someone who wants to be part of shaping how a university governs itself. What You’ll Bring You are a strategic and influential leader with the ability to navigate complex legal, governance and policy environments while building trusted relationships across a diverse stakeholder landscape. You bring a track record of providing high-level advice, exercising sound judgement and leading teams through change and complexity. Comfortable operating at both a strategic and operational level, you are motivated by the opportunity to lead a newly designed function and drive meaningful impact across the University. You will also bring: A tertiary qualification in Law and admission, or eligibility for admission, as an Australian Legal Practitioner. Significant leadership experience within legal, governance, policy, compliance or regulatory environments. Demonstrated experience providing strategic advice to executive leaders, governing bodies and senior stakeholders. Strong knowledge of governance, legislative and regulatory frameworks and the ability to balance risk, compliance and organisational outcomes. Experience leading and developing high-performing, multidisciplinary teams. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, communication and influencing skills. A commitment to fostering a culture that reflects UOW's Values in Action by leading with integrity, collaboration, inclusion and accountability. A passion for continuous improvement and building contemporary, customer-focused services that enable organisational success. As a member of the Integrity, Legal & Governance leadership team, you will play a critical role in supporting the University's strategic objectives and governance framework. Why Join UOW 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Fixed-term Full-time Opportunity | 5-Year Term Level 10 | Competitive salary on offer Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus / Hybrid Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply To apply for this position, you are required to submit a resume, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Morgan Bryant, General Counsel, Chief Assurance Officer & Secretary to Council on + 61 2 4239 5111 Closing Date: Sunday 4 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 7011 Job Category Legal & Compliance Posting Date 09/17/2026, 12:44 AM Apply Before 10/04/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Director, Legal and Policy - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
    }
